# CODEOWNERS — eInvite platform
#
# GitHub uses this file to automatically request review from the listed
# owners on any pull request that touches the matching paths.
#
# Replace `@maintainer` with the actual GitHub handle (or team slug, e.g.
# `@einvite/security-team`) before enabling branch protection. Documented in
# docs/security/CI-SECURITY.md §5 (CODEOWNERS policy).
#
# Syntax: <path-pattern> <owner1> <owner2> ...
# Last-matching pattern wins (like .gitignore).
# See https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# --- Security-critical Python paths ----------------------------------------
# Any change to the backend, the AI agent, or the platform services must be
# reviewed by the security maintainer — these paths touch auth, secrets,
# file upload, malware scanning, and the delivery channels.
src/python/                    @maintainer
ai_agent/                      @maintainer
platform_v32/                  @maintainer
future_platform_v52/           @maintainer

# --- Security module globs -------------------------------------------------
# The platform's password / passkey / malware-scan / auto-secret helpers are
# the highest-risk surface area. Explicitly listed so they don't slip through
# under the broader `src/python/` rule.
src/python/security_*.py        @maintainer
src/python/secrets_*.py         @maintainer

# --- Deploy + infra --------------------------------------------------------
# Dockerfiles, compose files, Caddyfile, install scripts — all affect the
# production blast radius. Owned by the security maintainer.
deploy/                        @maintainer

# --- CI / scripts ----------------------------------------------------------
# Don't let a PR silently weaken the CI gate. Every change to the security
# scan script, the SBOM generator, the CODEOWNERS file itself, or the CI
# workflow file requires maintainer review.
scripts/security-scan.sh       @maintainer
scripts/generate-sbom.py      @maintainer
.github/CODEOWNERS             @maintainer
.github/workflows/security.yml @maintainer
